  "rationale": "**Holds.** On `SessionStart`, `dispatch_builtin` -> `handle_session_start` includes `consent_hint`, which calls `discovery::pending_candidates`. That takes `discover(...).candidates`, which are the dependency-embedded plugins offered by the untrusted cargo transport (`active_plugins(dep_ids)`) that `decide` classifies as `Candidate`: not disabled (declined), not `use`d, not auto-enabled. It maps them to crate names and sorts and dedups them, so each dependency is named once. `consent_hint` returns `None` when the list is empty, otherwise it joins the names into the context. Other events never reach `consent_hint`.\n\n**Tests (pass):** `tests/enablement.rs::session_start_hints_pending_candidates` asserts the Claude `SessionStart` context contains `crate-a`. `tests/hook_stdout.rs::sync_progress_stays_off_hook_stdout` asserts the real binary's stdout contains `crate-a` for five agents. The \"once\" (dedup) part is judged from code; the fixture has a single candidate.\n\n**Refuted on review:** The builtin side computes the hint correctly, but the hint does not always reach the agent. In `execute_hook`, the builtin `SessionStart` output (which carries the consent hint) is passed to `dispatch_plugin_hooks` only as `prior_output`. If any active plugin's `SessionStart` hook exits 2 or is killed by a signal (no exit status), `dispatch_plugin_hooks` returns `Err(stderr)` (`None | Some(2) => return Err(child_out.stderr)`). `execute_hook` then answers with `blocked_response`, which for any event other than `PreToolUse` is `HookResponse::blocked(&reason)`: empty stdout, the reason on stderr and exit 2. So the builtin `additionalContext` is discarded and the pending dependencies are never named, even when the plugin hook simply crashed. Unlike `hooks.best_effort`, this requirement has no exception for a blocking plugin hook, so read plainly it is violated in that case. It conflicts with `hooks.exit_2_stops`, and the maintainer needs to decide: either add a \"unless a plugin hook blocks\" exception to the wording, or make the hint survive a block.\n",
  "requirement": "On `SessionStart`, when workspace dependencies ship plugins the user has neither enabled nor declined, Symposium MUST add context naming each of those dependencies once."
}
